; ============================================================
; WO-0 PIPELINE (concrete steps):
;   1. Input: this conversation (the compiler-framing session)
;   2. Extraction: done — this .wno file
;   3. Fold + query: verify graph captured decisions/constraints
;   4. Hand-render work order from the graph slice
;   5. Dispatch work order to a real backend (Claude Code or equiv)
;   6. Score: did constraints survive the trip? Where did drops
;      happen — extraction, rendering, or backend interpretation?
;
; OPEN QUESTIONS (resolve before or during WO-2):
;   q1: reconciliation report format (free-text? template? structured?)
;   q2: backend adapter contract (input/output/responsibilities)
;   q3: work-order rendering spec (sections, hop-count, context)
;   These don't block WO-0 — the hand-rendering step surfaces
;   what the format needs to be.
;
; KEY FRAMING (load-bearing for all downstream work):
;   - Winnow is a compiler from NL instructions to structured
;     work orders. Not a translator between "human" and "machine."
;   - The .wno graph is the IR. Fold is the optimization pass.
;     Work order is the emitted object code. Reconciliation is
;     runtime feedback from execution back to the compiler.
;   - Token efficiency at the dialogue/code boundary is the
;     economics argument; intent fidelity is the quality argument.
;   - Decisions are provisional. The graph records junctions.
;     "Never" language replaced by scope boundaries with revisit
;     triggers.
;   - Dialogue is code when it encodes instructions. The boundary
;     is representation and processing stage, not substance.
; ============================================================
